      "reference_sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM student_performance sp JOIN subject_details sd ON sd.subject = sp.subject WHERE sp.subject = 'CS303' AND ((sp.marks IS NULL OR sp.marks * 100.0 / sp.total_marks < CASE WHEN sd.subject_type = 'Lab' THEN 50 ELSE 40 END) OR sp.attendance < 75)",
      "notes": "All three sources: SS-1 defines the group, SQL counts it, the graph gives the dependent subjects (SS-5) and the bridge course with its coordinator (SS-4). CS303 is chosen because the three plausible wrong readings give three different counts: attendance only, failed only (forgetting the absentee), and failed-or-absent only."
